stories.body:
Microsoft's cloud just sped up. Azure grew 48% in the quarter, and @EconomyApp flagged the catch: about $10B of quarterly revenue is tied to OpenAI, quarterly capital spending is running near $45B, and free cash flow fell 27%. That makes one lab the single biggest swing factor in the biggest AI cloud.

@EvanKirstel put total revenue at $92.3B and said demand still exceeds supply, so CIOs should lock in capacity early. @holgermu noted the stock rose on the revenue beat. @dissectmarkets framed it across the hyperscalers: AWS near 40% growth, Google Cloud far higher, and none of it without the capex.

Why it matters: the AI boom's revenue is concentrated. If OpenAI shifts compute to other clouds or its own buildout, Azure's growth story shifts with it. Watch the next OpenAI compute deals, Microsoft's capex guidance, and whether free cash flow keeps falling as spending climbs.

SETI Institute and Breakthrough Listen use NVIDIA Holoscan and CUDA X to run agent driven observing for possible alien signals. Agentic control is moving into real scientific instruments.

@NVIDIAAI posted: "AI agents are now steering the Allen Telescope Array in Northern California to search for possible alien signals. Happy Halloween. Sleep tight. See how the @SETIInstitute and Breakthrough Listen are using NVIDIA Holoscan and CUDA X libraries to listen to the skies →"

@QwenAIFans added: "@NVIDIAAI @SETIInstitute AI agents steering a real telescope for SETI is peak Halloween. Holoscan plus CUDA X on the array is a wild production use." @jj_kovacs added: "@NVIDIAAI @SETIInstitute agents steering the dish is the part i'd look at. most of what a seti search picks up is our own phones and satellites, so the real job is deciding which blip is worth another hour of telescope time. if the agent gets that call wrong nobody ever knows what it skipped"

Coverage of Anthropic's S 1 highlights a reported $80B loss, while 2x Anthropic ETFs are filed but not yet live. First frontier lab IPO sets the public market read on AI lab economics.

@LifeboatHQ posted: "Anthropic Reports $80 Billion Loss in IPO Filing"

@kimmonismus added: "Another reason for open source. Unfortunately, Anthropic no longer allows good benchmarks like Minecraft or GTA 5 recreational games. To be fair: probably as a consequence of the IPO, to avoid legal issues due to copyright infringement." @signulll added: "at a $2t valuation & ~5,300 employees (per sept filing), anthropic effectively creates ~$377m in value per employee. so it’s now safe to say that we are entering an era where the scale of economic output will likely become pretty radically decoupled from the scale of human orgs."

Open weights DeepSeek V4.1 Flash tops Papers with Code usage as researchers build on it; resellers bundle cheap Flash access. Open frontier class weights are becoming the default research base.

@NielsRogge posted: "Unsurprisingly, DeepSeek v4.1 Flash is the most popular method on @paperswithcodee ! When you open source one of the best LLMs, all research gets built on top of it :)"

@CommandCodeAI added: "GOAT just made $100 credits PERMANENT On $10/mo plan DeepSeek V4.1 Flash 1017: $100 usage GLM 5.3 Flash: $100 usage GLM Flash casually doing 300 500 TPS in Command Code harness full weight models, btw" @UnslothAI added: "We’re releasing new DeepSeek V4.1 Flash 1017 GGUFs, ranking highest across benchmarks. Dynamic V3.1 leads across nearly all benchmarks: GPQA Diamond, AIME25, LiveCodeBench v6, MMLU Pro, Aider & more. Run on 64GB+ RAM. GGUF: Blog:"

After the FCC exempted Lightberry's Lumi from its foreign humanoid sales block on Oct 30, builders are picking apart its $39,990 price plus $20,000/yr software subscription. First humanoid cleared under the FCC rule sets the template for US humanoid pricing and compliance.

@IlirAliu_ posted: "Lightberry wants to charge $20,000 a year for software running on a $39,990 humanoid robot. That's $40,000 for the robot and another $40,000 in software fees over the following two years. Breakdown #002: @lightberry The San Francisco startup, founded by @aliattar and @sadkoeni"

@TheHumanoidHub added: "Lightberry’s Lumi is the first humanoid robot to receive Conditional Approval from the U.S. Government, earning an FCC exemption from the Covered List that blocks new foreign made robots from U.S. sale. The approval rests on two commitments:, Full replacement of sensors" @TheHumanoidHub added: "Check out the keynote from Do Park, Lightberry’s design chief, at the Humanoid Hub Conference. The evolution of relatability of humanoids will be very interesting to watch in coming years"

Amazon FAR, UC San Diego and Michigan researchers show humanoids using arms and torso as contact surfaces, not just hands. Whole body manipulation widens what humanoids can carry and reposition.

@XPeterKappes posted: "Researchers from Amazon FAR, UC San Diego, and the University of Michigan just introduced Whole Body Dexterity, a framework that lets humanoid robots grasp and reposition objects using their arms and torso as contact surfaces, not just their hands. Instead of limiting"

@CyberRobooo added: "What happens when robots start training inside a world model? Amazon FAR has an answer, DreamFAR, a real time interactive world model designed for robotic manipulation. It tackles a major challenge in robot simulation: keeping objects and their states consistent during long" @_bbelousov added: "Can a humanoid hold objects with its arms and torso, not just its hands? Whole Body Dexterity (WBD) from Amazon FAR, UCSD and Michigan does this on a real Unitree G1, carrying a box under one arm from a shelf to a table. In simulation, RL experts learn to move objects between"

Anthropic's Max 5x plan becomes Max ($100/month) and Max 20x becomes Ultra ($200/month); verified Ultra accounts lose the 5 hour usage window starting today. Users also report API credits bundled with the plans. Heavy Claude Code users were the most vocal about rate limits; removing the window on the top tier is a direct move in the coding agent pricing war with OpenAI.

@claudeai posted: "We’re renaming our Max plans: Max 5x → Max Max 20x → Ultra Max is still $100/month, and Ultra is still $200. If you’re a subscriber, there’s nothing you need to do. We’re also removing the 5 hour limit for verified Ultra accounts, starting today with most existing"

@tunguz added: "Look they too are jumping on the bandwagon of renaming things without any substantive underlying change." @StatsWire added: "Wait, Anthropic is giving Claude Max subscribers API credits now too? • Max 5x ($100/mo): $100 API credits • Max 20x ($200/mo): $200 API credits And you still get your regular Claude Code usage. OpenAI announced a similar benefit yesterday. Now Anthropic has it too. The API"

Moonshot AI launched 3D Make in Kimi, which connects to tools like Blender and CAD software to create 3D models, assemble scenes and develop games. It is available now on Kimi and Kimi Work. A day after adding Google workspace connectors, Kimi is pushing its agent into hands on creative and engineering software, where tool using agents are starting to compete.

@Kimi_Moonshot posted: "Introducing 3D Make in Kimi. Kimi connects to tools like Blender and CAD tools to create models, assemble scenes, and develop games. Available now on and Kimi Work."

@Kimi_Moonshot added: "How to get the most out of Kimi for 3D work? Here are 5 tips, and step by step walkthroughs:" @dicemanorama added: "Kimi just plugged itself into Blender and CAD. 3D Make has it build models, lay out scenes, even rough out games by driving the real tools. That should mean files you can actually open and tweak, not a mystery blob. The one person game studio just got a lot less lonely."

A new tour of Neuralink shows the R1 implant robot up close; separate reports say Neuralink is testing iPhone calls via its speech implant. BCI is moving from lab demos toward consumer device integration.

@cleoabram posted: "Full HUGE* If True episode on Neuralink and the future of brain computer interfaces I toured @neuralink and got a close up view of their new R1 surgical robot, to see the future they and @elonmusk are building and how it is already changing lives... 00:00 What if you put a"

@elonmusk added: "RT @Cyborg21: That's me. 72 hours of Neuralink engineers in my living room. Best part? Cheryl and I joked on the phone again. ALS sucks, m…" @neuralink added: "Neuralink devices are investigational and have not been approved by the FDA or other regulatory authorities. These videos feature voluntary clinical trial participants sharing their personal experiences, which may not reflect all participants or future outcomes."

OpenAI's CEO met Samsung leadership in Yongin on Oct 31, with talks centered on AI's impact on industry as memory supply tightens. Memory is the binding constraint on AI compute; OpenAI Samsung ties shape supply.

@digg posted: "OpenAI CEO Sam Altman met Samsung executives in South Korea as memory chip shortages deepen, with talks centered on AI’s impact on industry and business decisions over the next decade."

@sammygurus added: "Sam Altman met around 50 Samsung executives in South Korea and gave some of them OpenAI's Codex Micro Keyboard., Meeting held October 31 at Samsung's Human Resources Development Center in Yongin, Codex Micro Keyboard costs $230 and is currently sold out, 13 mechanical"

Students can now browse and add textbooks from OpenStax, S Chand and Open Textbook Library as NotebookLM sources at no charge. Google is locking in the student market by pairing its research notebook with licensed course material.

@Gemini_Notebook posted: "Calling all students: You can now access hundreds of textbooks directly in Notebook, for no charge. From publishers like S Chand Publishing, OpenStax, and Open Textbook Library, browse, select and upload them as sources to ace all of your upcoming exams (no more excuses, ok?)"

@loganthorneloe added: "RT @Gemini_Notebook: Calling all students: You can now access hundreds of textbooks directly in Notebook, for no charge. From publisher…"

Anthropic shipped Claude app upgrades: generated work opens beside the chat on iPad/iPhone, voice mode works in Apple CarPlay, and Claude on Android now behaves like a laptop app on Chromebooks and foldables. Puts Claude into the car and makes mobile a real work surface, sharpening the assistant race with ChatGPT and Gemini.

@claudeai posted: "A few upgrades to the Claude mobile apps this week: On iPad and iPhone Duo: what Claude makes now opens beside the chat instead of over it, and goes full screen when you want a closer look."

@adamlyttleapps added: "The iPad mini with 5g does a pretty good job imo I’ve removed X and Claude from my daily iPhone and I bring my iPad mini with me when I know I’ll be doing some work on the go Works well for me, shame it’s only 60hz though" @CodeByPoonam added: "FINALLY. Claude is in CarPlay. Now I can vibe code while driving."

Cartesia's new platform co designs its voice models and agent harness, claiming #1 on Artificial Analysis Speech Agent Arena and ServiceNow EVA Bench. Voice agents are moving from model APIs to full stack platforms; Cartesia is going after enterprise contact centers directly.

@cartesia posted: "Introducing Cartesia Managed Agents: our end to end voice agent platform for enterprise. #1 on @ArtificialAnlys Speech Agent Arena and @ServiceNow EVA Bench, built by co designing our voice models and harness as one system. Check it out →"

@Ayzacoder added: "RT @cartesia: Introducing Cartesia Managed Agents: our end to end voice agent platform for enterprise. #1 on @ArtificialAnlys Speech Agent…" @EyubogluSabri added: "RT @krandiash: We’re having a helluva week, announcing our new platform for voice agents, Managed Agents At Cartesia, we’ve always believ…"

Per Quanta, OpenAI did not release a result claiming to make a particle physics theory rigorous; physicists are now working through the proof. A test case for how AI produced mathematics gets verified before anyone claims a breakthrough.

@QuantaMagazine posted: "On the advice of a group of physicists, OpenAI hasn’t released a major result that claims to make a theory in particle physics mathematically rigorous. Instead, the physicists are now working to understand the 1,147 page AI proof themselves."

@QuantaMagazine added: "OpenAI’s disproof of the exponential time hypothesis came as a surprise to many. Researchers hope to explore whether the result will lead to progress on the broader “P = NP” problem, arguably the most important question in theoretical computer science." @CFDevelop added: "I think Terence Tao is becoming one of my favourite thinkers to listen to. I never really paid much attention to math until I started digging deeper into functional programming, but through the research on Osprey and now the novel proofs from OpenAI, he's helping make sense"

Mistral AI published open weights for Mistral Large 4 ("Le Chonk"), reported as a ~1T parameter mixture of experts with 49B active. Artificial Analysis ranks it the top open weights model built outside China, and vLLM with NovaSky's SkyRL shipped day 0 RL support on the NVFP4 checkpoint. A frontier scale open model from Europe resets the open weights field outside China and gives builders a new base to fine tune.

@vllm_project posted: "Day 0 RL for @MistralAI’s Mistral Large 4 with @NovaSkyAI’s SkyRL and @vllm_project! On 8 @nvidia GB200 nodes, LoRA RL on the NVFP4 checkpoint brings AIME 2024 avg@8 from ~64% to ~75% in 75 training steps. vLLM generates rollouts, while FSDP2 or Megatron handles training."

@caffeineai added: "We've just added Mistral Large 4 to Caffeine. It's Mistral's largest most capable model yet. Use it to build a new app or keep improving one you've already started. On Caffeine, its credit price is lower than Claude Sonnet 5.5's. You'll find it in the model menu, and you can" @support_huihui added: "Next ablation target model: mistralai/Mistral Large 4 1T A52B Let’s see how difficult it is to ablate. On Agentic Coding, it’s roughly comparable to GLM5.3."

Cursor said a modified, malicious version of the Claude Code VS Code extension was distributed through the Cursor IDE extension marketplace, affecting at most 5,000 users. Cursor says the tampered build was not made by Anthropic and that other extensions are not impacted. A supply chain attack through an AI coding IDE's extension store shows how agent tooling with deep repo and shell access has become a prime target for attackers.

@cursor_ai posted: "We identified a security incident affecting a modified Claude Code VS Code extension accessed through our Cursor IDE extension marketplace, impacting at most 5,000 users. This malicious version of the extension was not developed by Anthropic. It does not impact other extensions"

@mert added: "normies aren't aware yet but we are actually living through the movie Terminator atm for cybersecurity without exaggeration just absolutely relentless revenge of the machines" @felixrieseberg added: "We’re working with Cursor on this incident, but it wasn’t a compromise of Anthropic’s systems or employee laptops. A malicious actor used access to Cursor’s marketplace to publish a tampered copy of the Claude Code extension, which we didn’t build or publish. The versions on our"

The product plays the same sentence in a human and an AI voice and asks listeners to pick. Top text to speech models are near human parity.

@Scobleizer posted: "The best AI voices are getting hard to tell apart from each other. Not from humans. @shobhitbanga and @voicearena_ai just launched Turing TTS. Same sentence twice, one human one AI. Listeners try to pick the human. Fool Rate is how often they pick the AI instead. In this"

@cartesia added: "Sonic 3.6: Numéro un & Nummer eins Ranked #1 among real time models for Customer Support on @voicearena_ai’s French and German leaderboards." @voicearena_ai added: "Cartesia's Sonic 3.6 ranks #1 among real time models in Customer Support on both the Voice Arena French and German TTS Leaderboards. Sonic 3.6 from @cartesia is a real time TTS model built for enterprise workloads at scale. Every ranking on Voice Arena comes from blind"

&Tutor scored best on a widely used tutor model eval, the company says. A product launch betting on modeling humans, not just tasks.

@humansand posted: "Introducing Ampersand Tutor (&Tutor), we trained a model to learn like people, then trained &Tutor to teach it On a widely used tutor model eval, &Tutor performed best, showing how better models of people can help build AI for humans Available through our API, try it!"

@viamrobotics added: "We’re going live with @nvidia on Thursday, Nov 5 at 11 AM PT to walk through the tutorial step by step. Join us:" @joinHandshake added: "Congratulations to @humansand on the launch of &Tutor! &Tutor is a model trained to teach models the way humans teach. It's great to see our dataset being used to improve AI tutors and student simulators in their work. In our ATLAS Education study of 2,800+ students, we found"

Dutch startup Monumental used its bricklaying robots to build a full building with curved walls and mixed bonds. Construction robotics moving from demos to finished buildings.

@clankrmedia posted: "Robots laid every brick of this building. Dutch startup Monumental built it in Almere. Curved walls, mixed brick types and bonds, even lettering. Its founder says 15 more houses follow in the coming weeks."

@AGkorthos added: "These robots are doing real construction work. Developed by Dutch company @BuildMonumental, they work together to build brick walls, including curved structures and intricate decorative patterns."

Observers expect only a 27B Qwen4 model to be released open weight, not the full lineup. Alibaba's open weight strategy has shaped the open model ecosystem; a pullback would matter.

@bnjmn_marie posted: "Many seem to think that the announced Qwen4 models will be open weight We will probably only get the 27B I'm not sure we will get flash"

@0xBakeer added: "qwen's own model card calls qwen3.8 flash next an experimental preview of the architecture behind qwen4. so running flash next on my spark is already the closest thing to qwen4 prep"

3D OS gives coding agents 80 skills across animation, rigging, art and previs. Agents are being packaged for creative 3D pipelines.

@emmanuel_2m posted: "We just open sourced an entire 3D studio. Introducing 3D OS by Scenario. It gives your coding agent 6 departments and 80 skills. 3D OS ┃ ┣ Animation ┃ ┣ Rigging Any Character ┃ ┗ Motion From a Video ┃ ┣ Art ┃ ┣ Previs and Storyboards ┃ ┗"

@conorsen added: "From a scenario analysis standpoint, trying to put myself in the headspace next Wednesday of 53 54 Dem Senators and a bigger AI selloff to think about what the takes and algo content will be doing." @livekit added: "We ran @MistralAI's Voxtral 3 through LiveKit Simulations with the same agent, same scenarios, over real audio. Check out the results. And start building today:"

Runway's Agent opens files, runs code, and produces product shots, ad variations and motion graphics. Creative AI tools are becoming full agents, not just generators.

@runwayml posted: "Introducing new capabilities in Runway Agent Now, Agent does more than generate. It can open files and run code, it builds your brands launch kit and creates product shots, ad variations, motion graphics from a reference and more. Whatever you need, Agent gets it done."

@IXITimmyIXI added: "Do not get caught sleeping on the new Runway Agent.. it's incredible what you can do with it" @WillVI added: "Gemini 3.8 Flash Text to Speech is now available at @runwayml across Tool, Agent & Workflows. 2,000+ voices, 30 languages. Just describe the delivery. Example: calm and reassuring, firm, like a news anchor."

Sternstein argues technical hiring is running hot and the AI jobs panic is not showing up in postings. A data counterpoint to the AI layoffs narrative from a major AI investor.

@a16z posted: "a16z's Moses Sternstein on the AI jobs panic, what job postings actually show, and why technical hiring is running hot: "People are saying, 'Oh, AI's already killing jobs.'... but right now it's almost certainly not." "Even human resources, right? Which is considered the front"

@mentorcapital1 added: "@herbertong This is only useful if the use sustainable energy we use G Air to schedule large AI jobs and it redirects jobs to data centers that use Solar only and keeps a verified carbon accounting ledger to maintain our Carbon negative status. Lots of Cities will run digital twins this way" @MunshiPremChnd added: "Netflix is tackling GPU reliability like a distributed systems challenge! See how layered health checks, automated fixes, and fault tolerant training keep AI jobs running despite hardware failures:"

Developers can set up ElevenLabs with one prompt to a coding agent, which runs the CLI and adds the API key. Dev tools are being redesigned for coding agents as the main user.

@ElevenLabsDevs posted: "Our onboarding is now agent first. You can set up ElevenLabs in your environment with one prompt to your coding agent. The agent runs the ElevenLabs CLI and adds an API key to your project. Your only manual step is clicking Authorize in the browser."

@smallest_AI added: "Pulse Pro is the #1 speech to text model for English accuracy. On Bluejay Labs' independent MISTT benchmark, it outperformed 82 other models on real voice agent calls and doctor patient consults, including Amazon, NVIDIA, ElevenLabs and Deepgram. See the full leaderboard in the" @smallest_AI added: "MISTT tests what voice agents actually hear: phone lines, noise and a second speaker talking over the caller. With background speech, Pulse Pro picked up 0.7% of the other speaker’s words. ElevenLabs Scribe v2: 24.3%. Full results:"

ElevenLabs' new sound effects model generates more layered, precise effects from a single prompt, with improved music and vocals. Generative audio keeps closing the gap with stock libraries for film, games and ads.

@ElevenLabs posted: "Big scenes rarely come down to one sound, so we built SFX v3 to handle more than ever. Our latest model lets you create richer, more precise sound effects from a single text prompt, with improved music and vocals. Now available inside @ElevenCreative and ElevenAPI."

@ElevenLabsDevs added: "Introducing SFX v3 for developers. SFX v3 gives developers more control over the detail, context, and character of every generation compared to v2." @ElevenLabs added: "Listen for the umpire. SFX v3 gets every part of the prompt right, with richer and more precise audio and voices."

The model handles duplex conversation with ~400ms end to end latency, fusing vision and speech on device. Real time, local interaction is a prerequisite for humanoids working around people.

@TheHumanoidHub posted: "AGIBOT just announced WITA Omni 1.0: an omni modal interaction model, Duplex conversation: listening and speaking at the same time, Runs on device, with end to end interaction latency of ~400ms, Fuses vision, speech, real time dialogue, facial expressions and physical actions"

@FutureAZA added: "@ElectricRob @DrKnowItAll16 Naw, you just needed a story to accompany it." @xmercury_one added: "@TheHumanoidHub ~400 ms on device is already close to a natural pause. In a 2009 study, people started answering within about 200 ms, so 400ms is pretty close. We will get there in a few months"

Autonomous ship maker Saronic is among a16z's list of companies rebuilding US industry and defense. A guide to where defense tech money is flowing.

@Saronic posted: "Saronic is proud to be recognized as one of the Top 50 companies that are rebuilding and protecting America on a16z’s 2026 American Dynamism’s list. Thanks to @a16z team for the recognition. We’re just getting started."

@Astranis added: "Astranis is proud to be named to a16z’s 2026 American Dynamism 50, a list of companies rebuilding and protecting America. From our factory at San Francisco’s Pier 70, we’re building MicroGEO satellites that provide nations and operators dedicated, sovereign connectivity." @jimbelosic added: "41 out of 50 are scs customers. American Dynamism runs on sheet metal and billet"

Mathematicians on X report a deterministic, worst case subexponential bound for integer factorization, extending an AI assisted (Claude) ETH refutation; the Lean formalization was audited, with errors noted in the English proof. If it holds, an AI assisted result just moved one of the foundations of cryptography and complexity theory. That is AI doing frontier math, not chat.

@ElliotGlazer posted: "In case you missed it, integer factorization has been proven subexponential (deterministically, worst case bound)! The hard work comes from Claude's version of the ETH refutation but it seems a little more had to be done to get this result for integer factorization."

@ElliotGlazer added: "I had Astra audit the result. The Lean certifies exactly what it says it does, though the English proof has some errors." @StefanoMTessaro added: "I wonder whether people realize just how many cryptographic constructions may now admit subexponential time attacks, assuming the new ETH results hold up. (Result obtained from a one shot Astra query, obviously unverified.)"

TBC's image to video model mischief 1 starts at 0.5 cents a second and is now on Design Arena. A cheap new entrant in AI video generation from an unusual lab.

@AlexKsendzovsky posted: "today, we introduce a little mischief to the world. for four years, we’ve been brewing real brain cells on electrodes to understand how they compute. now, we’ve turned those discoveries into a video model anyone can use. from 0.5¢ a second, mischief 1 is at least 5x faster than"

@WonderStudiosX added: "At Wonder, we're lucky to be working with some of the most frontier companies in the world, pushing boundaries of what's possible TBC's model, Mischief, uses real lab grown neurons to make video generation faster and cheaper A pleasure to work with the team to bring this vision" @OpenRouter added: "A little mischief for Halloween mischief 1 from The Biological Computing Co. turns an image into video, using four years of research on real brain cells grown on electrodes. From $0.005 a second, live now on OpenRouter."

The r187 release of Three.js adds light probe speedups, UV unwrapping and light baking, and moves WebGPU rendering out of experimental territory. Three.js underpins most 3D on the web, so solid WebGPU support raises the ceiling for browser based 3D and spatial apps.

@threejs posted: "Three.js r187 released"

@threejs added: "Featured examples: New Light Map Baker Faster LightProbeGrid Baking New Occlusion Dither New VDBLoader New WebGPU Path Tracer Improved ClusteredLighting" @benhouston3d added: "New #ThreeJs release with my light probe speed ups, uv unwrapping, light baking features!"

SpeRID Labs released Idol, a 600M parameter 3D diffusion transformer trained from scratch that runs in under 7.2GB of VRAM. Small, open 3D generators make asset creation cheap for games, AR and spatial apps.

@speridlabs posted: "Meet Idol, an open image to 3D model. A 3D DiT that generates complete 3D objects from just an image. Pre trained from scratch, contains only 600M parameters, it runs on consumer GPUs, using less than 7.2 GB of VRAM and can generate 1M splats in 3 seconds. Try it today. Fully"

@speridlabs added: "Want your own 3D Funko Pop? Reply with a photo of anything (you, your pet, etc.) and we'll turn it into a Funko figure with Idol, our image to 3D model. The Funko with most likes gets 3D printed and sent to the winner." @ivanfioravanti added: "Idol Image to 3D model is amazing! So I decided to port it to Apple MLX on the fly! There are some pieces still in MPS and more optimizations to bring in, step by step Thanks for this amazing model @speridlabs Here it is:"

a16z's Alex Rampell and Eve CEO Jay Madheswaran discuss how AI lets plaintiff firms take cases that were too small to be worth a lawyer's time. Legal AI is one of a16z's biggest bets on AI changing the unit economics of a service business.

@a16z posted: "If a case won't earn a lawyer at least $5,000 in fees, most won't take it. AI is starting to change that math. Eve co founder and CEO Jay Madheswaran joins a16z's Alex Rampell to explain how AI can automate plaintiff law from the first client call through settlement, and how one"

@evelegalai added: "Think about giving David a slingshot to take down Goliath. That's what we're doing." @jayanthmadhesw1 joined @arampell on the @a16z podcast to talk about how Eve is helping level the playing field for plaintiff firms across the nation." @dhaber added: "RT @a16z: If a case won't earn a lawyer at least $5,000 in fees, most won't take it. AI is starting to change that math. Eve co founder an…"

Subvocal's glasses bounce radar off lip and jaw muscles to transcribe silently mouthed words at 200+ words per minute, with no audio or cameras; preorders are open. A new AI input interface getting early backing; silent speech could matter for wearables where talking out loud fails.

@Scobleizer posted: "I hate talking into my computer in a cafe. @AarushYadav47 raised $1.3M from YC and Afore for Subvocal. Glasses that bounce radar off your lip and jaw muscles and turn silent mouthing into text at over 200 words a minute. No sound. No keyboard. No cameras. Preorders:"

@kimmonismus added: "Subvocal is building glasses that turn silently mouthed words into text. The team says its prototypes can do 200+ words per minute. That is super fascinating and an incredible achievement. I'm curious how well they handle the little corrections you make mid sentence." @ritwikpavan added: "NEW: Subvocal built smart glasses that let you talk to your computer without making a sound. The glasses turn deliberately mouthed words into text, so you can write messages or talk to AI without speaking out loud or touching a keyboard., Company says prototypes can exceed"

SemiAnalysis breaks down die to wafer hybrid bonding methods presented at Semicon West. Advanced packaging is a bottleneck for AI accelerators and HBM.

@SemiAnalysis_ posted: "In Semicon west this year, there was a lot of buzz around hybrid bonding. EV group presented hybrid bonding as an important technique accelerating 3D integration and advanced packaging. They presented two major methods to perform die to wafer hybrid bonding which are direct"

@SemiAnalysis_ added: "In direct placement, singulated dies on a film frame get cleaned and plasma activated, then a flip chip bonder places them one at a time onto the activated target wafer. In collective die to wafer, dies are picked and placed onto a reconstituted carrier wafer which is then" @AIEngineRoom added: "@SemiAnalysis_ Collective die to wafer going through a reconstituted carrier wafer is an interesting split from direct placement. Which of the two do you expect fabs to favor first for high volume?"

Pika says H3 Flex tops DesignArena's open weight text to video board, with 4K output and audio stems. Open weight video models are closing on closed ones.

@Axylusion posted: ".@pika_labs launched Pika H3 Flex. They say it sits at number one among open weight text to video models on DesignArena's board, with exportable audio stems, up to 4K, and a 15 second clip with soundtrack in as little as 7 seconds. Weights are out from day one. Vendor"

@ComfyUI added: "A Halloween music video made with Pika's new H3 Flex model Now in ComfyUI with 6 step video generation, synchronized audio, and reference guided generation. To try this workflow, link below" @hyperbolic_labs added: "A toast to @pika_labs on Pika H3 Flex Open weights, 4K, faster than realtime. Congrats @chenlin_meng @demi_guo_ and team!"

MediaTek says Q4 revenue grows 30% q/q to $6.8B, driven by $2.5B in AI ASIC chips, above its $2B guide. Custom AI chips are becoming a second front against Nvidia GPUs.

@SKundojjala posted: "MediaTek 4Q26, Revenue up 9.1% q/q and 10.7% y/y to $5.25B at 46.3% GM; 4Q26 revenue will grow by 30% q/q to $6.8B, driven by ASIC, $2.5B AI ASIC revenue in 4Q (vs prior $2B guidance); started shipping from Sep, 2027 ASIC is now at the high end of the $16B target (20% of the"

@SKundojjala added: "DC GM below the company average but OPM accretive like typical ASIC business, Mobile 37% of revenue,, 1% q/q and, 17% y/y. Flagships did better vs rest of the portfolio, Smart Edge 58% of revenue, +20% q/q and +63% y/y; 5G thin modem (Google/Xiaomi), AI tablets/PCs, car"

